        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Order by the machine, not by guesswork.</strong> Use the model
            and serial number to get the right belt, measure the loop rather than the deck if you
            must, and check the deck while the belt is off — a new belt on a worn deck is money
            spent twice.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The fitting itself is an afternoon with basic tools and a helper. What makes it last is
            the setup:
            <a href="/how-tight-should-treadmill-belt-be/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">tension by the lift test</a>,
            centre it on a slow empty run, follow the manual on lubrication, and
            <strong class="text-white">recheck both after break-in</strong>.
          </p>
        </div>
